BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Ostrava//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Ostrava — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Svíčková — Beef sirloin in a cream-and-root-vegetable sauce\, with dumplings and cranberries.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SVEECH-ko-vah. The Czech Sunday dish\, on a weekday lunch menu: 195 CZK on 21 Oct 2026. Best: Ostrawica Lokál\, Masarykovo náměstí
LOCATION:Ostrawica Lokál\, Masarykovo náměstí
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ostrawica+Lok%C3%A1l+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Roast goose with lokše — St Martin's goose with red and white cabbage and potato flatbreads.
DESCRIPTION:Say: LOK-sheh. The November feast\; Harenda serves it inside the mining museum\, 6–17 Nov. Best: Harenda U Barborky\, Landek Park
LOCATION:Harenda U Barborky\, Landek Park
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Harenda+U+Barborky+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Smoked beef tongue with horseradish — Smoked tongue\, horseradish sauce\, dumpling.
DESCRIPTION:Say: oo-ZEH-nee ya-ZIK. The serious pub plate of the Czech lands. Best: Stará kuželna
LOCATION:Stará kuželna
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Star%C3%A1+ku%C5%BEelna+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Dršťková polévka — Tripe soup with paprika and marjoram.
DESCRIPTION:Say: DRSHT-ko-vah. The working man's soup\, on the weekly menu. Best: Stará kuželna
LOCATION:Stará kuželna
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Star%C3%A1+ku%C5%BEelna+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ostravar — The city's own pale lager.
DESCRIPTION:Say: OS-tra-var. Brewed in Ostrava since 1898 — until 2027\, when brewing moves to Prague. Best: Any Ostrava pub this winter — the brewery has no public tap
LOCATION:Any Ostrava pub this winter — the brewery has no public tap
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ostravar+pivovar+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Štramberské uši — Honey gingerbread rolled into a cone.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SHTRAM-ber-skeh OO-shee. EU-protected since 2007\; about a dozen licensed bakers. Best: The square in Štramberk — buy them fresh\, not in sealed bags
LOCATION:The square in Štramberk — buy them fresh\, not in sealed bags
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C5%A0tramberk+n%C3%A1m%C4%9Bst%C3%AD
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Valašský frgál — A broad\, thin Wallachian tart with one filling — poppy seed\, curd or pear.
DESCRIPTION:Say: VA-lash-skee FR-gahl. EU-protected since 2013. Best: Wallachian bakeries south of Ostrava\, Rožnov and Frenštát
LOCATION:Wallachian bakeries south of Ostrava\, Rožnov and Frenštát
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ro%C5%BEnov+pod+Radho%C5%A1t%C4%9Bm
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kyselica — Sauerkraut soup with potatoes and sausage.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KI-se-li-tsa. The woodcutter's breakfast of the Beskydy. Best: Beskydy pubs — Pustevny and the ridge
LOCATION:Beskydy pubs — Pustevny and the ridge
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pustevny
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vdolek — A round Czech yeast pastry\, filled.
DESCRIPTION:Say: VDO-lek. An old Czech pastry beside French charcuterie on the same menu. Best: HogoFogo Bistro (weekdays)
LOCATION:HogoFogo Bistro (weekdays)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=HogoFogo+Bistro+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rozpečené tvarůžky — Baked ripe Olomouc cheese.
DESCRIPTION:Say: TVA-roozh-kee. The Czech pub snack with the strongest smell\, beside a 60-day dry-aged steak. Best: Stračena Garden\, Svinov
LOCATION:Stračena Garden\, Svinov
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Stra%C4%8Dena+Garden+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Phở bò — Beef noodle soup\, the northern Vietnamese way.
DESCRIPTION:Say: fuh baw. The Czech default bowl since the 2000s. Best: Happy Banh Mi\, Masarykovo náměstí
LOCATION:Happy Banh Mi\, Masarykovo náměstí
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Happy+Banh+Mi+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vareniky — Potato-filled dumplings.
DESCRIPTION:Say: va-RE-nee-kee. Pelmeni and vareniky in a shop open since 2018. Best: Pelmeški
LOCATION:Pelmeški
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pelme%C5%A1ki+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Chuť Beskyd — The Taste of the Beskydy tasting menu.
DESCRIPTION:Say: khoot BES-kid. The region's only Bib Gourmand cooking Beskydy farmers' produce. Best: MIURA\, Čeladná
LOCATION:MIURA\, Čeladná
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=MIURA+%C4%8Celadn%C3%A1+%C4%8Cesko
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Fallow deer with gingerbread — Venison\, gingerbread\, black pepper\, berries.
DESCRIPTION:A Czech larder rewritten by a MICHELIN-selected kitchen. Best: Cattaleya\, Čeladná
LOCATION:Cattaleya\, Čeladná
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cattaleya+%C4%8Celadn%C3%A1+%C4%8Cesko
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Radegast from the tower — The bitter lager of Moravia\, tasted at the end of the tour.
DESCRIPTION:Say: RA-de-gast. Brewed at Nošovice since 1970\, with the Beskydy in view. Best: Pivovar Radegast\, Nošovice
LOCATION:Pivovar Radegast\, Nošovice
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pivovar+Radegast%2C+No%C5%A1ovice+No%C5%A1ovice+%C4%8Cesko
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:A chateau house lager — A seasonal beer brewed in the chateau.
DESCRIPTION:Five centuries of brewing on the record\; brewing again since 2007. Best: Zámek Zábřeh
LOCATION:Zámek Zábřeh
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Z%C3%A1mek+Z%C3%A1b%C5%99eh+Pivovar+Pikard+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Batch brew at the station — Specialty coffee at a kiosk on the platform concourse.
DESCRIPTION:kafeKostka has served Ostrava-Svinov's commuters every day since 2014. Best: Laura Coffee — kafeKostka\, Svinov station
LOCATION:Laura Coffee — kafeKostka\, Svinov station
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Laura+Coffee+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Breakfast under the gold ceiling — A croissant Benedikt in a restored First Republic café.
DESCRIPTION:Restored in 2012\, and still ordinary prices. Best: Kavárna Elektra (weekdays)
LOCATION:Kavárna Elektra (weekdays)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kav%C3%A1rna+Elektra+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Turkish eggs — Poached eggs\, yoghurt\, chilli butter.
DESCRIPTION:The city's brunch\, named by a local promoter. Best: Drinkeat
LOCATION:Drinkeat
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Drinkeat+Ostrava
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:ostrava-liste-20@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Natural wine by the glass — Organic and natural bottles from growers the owners know.
DESCRIPTION:Twenty years in conventional wine before they switched. Best: HokusPokus (Tue–Sat)
LOCATION:HokusPokus (Tue–Sat)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=HokusPokus+Ostrava
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
